{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David. Vindicate me.</b> Rabbi Moses said: the meaning of שפטני is: take up my case and do justice for me against my enemies. The correct interpretation in my eyes: its meaning is, take up the case from me, if my heart has turned away from after You, therefore 'for I walk in my integrity' (תמים), like 'you shall be wholehearted' (תמים תהיה)." "<b>And in YHWH I trusted.</b> That He help me so that my heart be whole; therefore 'I shall not slip' (לא אמוט)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:37.039208637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}